When an iframe’s loading attribute changes from lazy to eager, Ladybird
runs its pending lazy load resumption steps, so the iframe loads
right away, and stops intersection-observing it. The other engines
all do the same. Gecko’s HTMLIFrameElement::AfterSetAttr() calls
StopLazyLoading(TriggerLoad::Yes) when the old value was lazy. For any
value but lazy, WebKit’s HTMLIFrameElement::attributeChanged() calls
LazyLoadElementObserver::unobserve() and then loadDeferredFrame(). And
for an eager value, Blink’s HTMLFrameOwnerElement::ParseAttribute()
calls LazyLoadFrameObserver::LoadImmediately().
